From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: an8855: leave room for a second 802.1Q tag

The switch's global RX length (GMACCR) is sized for one tag: MTU +
ETH_HLEN + MTK_TAG_LEN + ETH_FCS_LEN, 1522 bytes at MTU 1500. The
an8855-8021q tagger sends a VLAN upper's frame with its own tag only, so
a port and a single VLAN upper of it fit. A VLAN upper of a VLAN upper
(QinQ, wan.20.30) is [20][30] on the CPU link and on the wire: a
1500-byte packet makes a 1526-byte frame.

The switch drops such frames at the MAC RX of the port they enter, the
CPU port included, and counts them in RxBadPktBytes. Measured on a
Xiaomi AX3000T v2 with wan.20.30 at MTU 1500: pings passed up to a
1522-byte frame and failed from 1523, and TCP over the QinQ interface
moved no data in either direction, on the host path and offloaded alike
(ECM installs the rules, the switch drops the frames). With this patch
every size passed, the drop counters stayed at 0, and TCP ran at 936
Mbit/s each way, offloaded.

Add one VLAN_HLEN, which selects the 1536-byte setting at MTU 1500. Do it
in either tag mode: the NSS bring-up switches the conduit from mtk to
an8855-8021q at run time, after DSA programmed the CPU port's MTU, and
the register is only rewritten on an MTU change. (A version that added
the tag in 8021q mode only was measured to change nothing for that
reason.) From reading the code, not measured: a customer-tagged frame
through a VLAN-unaware bridge carries two tags as well, and so does a
QinQ frame in mtk mode.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/an8855.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/an8855.c
@@ -1446,6 +1446,11 @@ an8855_port_change_mtu(struct dsa_switch
 
 	/* RX length also includes Ethernet header, MTK tag, and FCS length */
 	length = new_mtu + ETH_HLEN + MTK_TAG_LEN + ETH_FCS_LEN;
+	/* ...and a second 802.1Q tag, for QinQ: the limit applies at every
+	 * port's MAC RX, the CPU port included. In either tag mode, since the
+	 * tagger can change at run time without this being rewritten.
+	 */
+	length += VLAN_HLEN;
 	if (length <= 1522)
 		val = AN8855_MAX_RX_PKT_1518_1522;
 	else if (length <= 1536)
